C o m p i l a t i o n


      Title Optimization model for Glen Canyon Dam releases to favor Bugs popula
      tion. (Market and contract pricing April 2018)
       
      ###################################
      Created By: Moazzam Ali Rind
      Email: moazzamalirind@gmail.com
       
      Created : 12/16/2020
      Last updated: 4/11/2022
       
      Description: This model was developed to qaunitfy the trade-off between nu
      mber of steady low flow days and hydropower revenue objectives.
                  The model has 2 periods per day (i.e. pHigh and plow), three d
      istinct day types(Sunday,Saturday, and Weekday) and runs for a month. we h
      ave used linear programming to solve the problem.
                  All the structural and operational constraints for Glen Canyon
       Dam applied here are uptodate.
       
      ######################################
  17   
  18  ****Model code
  19   
  20  Set
  21            d                             Types of Days involved in the mode
      l/Sunday, Saturday, Weekday/
  22            FlowPattern                   Types of flow pattern in the model
       /Steady,Hydropeak/
  23            p                             Periods during a day /pLow "Low fl
      ow period",pHigh "High flow period"/
  24            tot_vol                       Total montly release volume scenar
      ios (acre-ft)/V1*V3/
  25            modpar                        Saving model status for each of th
      e scenario solution/ ModStat "Model Status", SolStat "Solve Status"/
  26            Nu_SteadyDays                 Defining constrainted cases for nu
      mber of low flow steady days /case1*case12/
  27            Price                         Pricing type ($ per MWh)/Contract,
       Market/
  28            Offset                        Scenarios of offset releases betwe
      en off-peak Hydropeak day and steady day releases /H1*H4/
  29  ;
  30   
  31   
  32  * Alias create imageo f the set.
  33  Alias (d,Days);
  34  Alias (FlowPattern,FlowType);
  35   
  36  *======================================
  37  Parameters
  38  *======================================
  39   
  40  Initstorage                           Initial reservoir storage (e.g Stora
      ge in Powell on 1st April 2018) (acre-ft)/12948951/
  41  * Storage data for lake Powell can be found at: http://lakepowell.water-da
      ta.com/index2.php
  42   
  43  Inflow                                Average monthly Inflow to reservoir 
      (cfs) /7049.94/
  44  *Inflow data can be found at: http://lakepowell.water-data.com/index2.php
  45   
  46  maxstorage                            Maximumn Reservoir capacity (acre-ft
      )/25000000/
  47  minstorage                            Minimum reservoir storage to maintai
      n hydropower level(acre-ft)/5892163/
  48  maxRel                                Maximum release in a day d at any ti
      meperiod p(cfs) /32000/
  49  minRel                                Minimum release in a day d at any ti
      meperiod p(cfs)/8000/
  50  evap                                  Evaporation (ac-ft per Month) /24695
      /
  51  *The evaporation data can be found at: https://www.usbr.gov/rsvrWater/Hist
      oricalApp.html
  52   
  53   
  54  Duration(p)                           Duration of period (hours)
  55  Vol_monthlyrelease(tot_vol)           Different monthyl release Volumes (a
      cre-ft)/V1 719449.7,V2 827034,V3 944701.8/
  56  TotMonth_volume                       To represent total monthly volume (a
      cre-ft)
  57   
  58  Num_Days(FlowPattern,d)               To represent different number of day
       types
  59   
  60   
  61  Saturdays(FlowPattern,d)              To represent the number of saturdays
       (i.e. steady flow saturdays and unsteady flow saturdays)
  62  Sundays(FlowPattern,d)                To represent the number of Sundays (
      i.e. steady flow sundays and unsteady flow sundays)
  63  Weekdays(FlowPattern,d)               To represent the number of weekdays 
      (i.e. steady flow weekdays and unsteady flow weekdays)
  64   
  65  Weekend_Rel                           Additional release made on weekend o
      ff-peak incomparison to weekday off-peak release(cfs).
  66  Diff_Release(Offset)                  Differnce between off-peak weekday r
      elease and weekend release(cfs)/H1 0, H2 500, H3 750, H4 1000/
  67   
  68   
  69  FStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays)                          Storing obje
      ctive function values over different scenarios ($$)
  70   
  71  XStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days)            Store Energy
       Generated during different types of days over different cases (MWh)
  72  RStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days,p)          Store Releas
      e values during different types of days over different cases (cfs)
  73  Sstore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays)                          Store Storag
      e Values over different cases(ac-ft)
  74   
  75  ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,modpar)             Store soluti
      on status of the scenarios i.e. whether the solution found is optimal or n
      ot?
  76   
  77  Rev(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days,p)             Revenue ($$)
  78  Observed_Rel(Days,p)                                          Observed hyd
      ropeaking releases for day types during periods.
  79   
  80  ;
  81   
  82  Duration("pLow")= 8;
  83  * low period weightage in a day(08 Hours or 8 by 24 i.e:0.33 of day)
  84   
  85  Duration("pHigh")= 16;
  86  *  High period weightage in a day( 16 Hours or 16 by 24 i.e:0.67 of day)
  87   
  88  Table Days_Distribution(FlowType,Days,Nu_SteadyDays) "number of steady and
       unsteady saturdays sundays and weekdays in the month"
  89                           case1   case2   case3   case4   case5   case6  ca
      se7   case8   case9   case10   case11   case12
  90  Steady. Sunday            0       1        2       4      4        4      
      4       4       4       4         4         4
  91  Hydropeak. Sunday         4       3        2       0      0        0      
      0       0       0       0         0         0
  92  Steady. Saturday          0       0        0       0      2        4      
      4       4       4       4         4         4
  93  Hydropeak. Saturday       4       4        4       4      2        0      
      0       0       0       0         0         0
  94  Steady. Weekday           0       0        0       0      0        0      
      1       2       7       12        17        22
  95  Hydropeak. Weekday        22      22       22      22     22       22     
      21      20      15      10        5         0     ;
  96   
  97  Table Energy_Price(d,Price,p)"Price of MegaWatt hour during different days
       and within period p ($ per MWh)"
  98                        pLow        pHigh
  99  Sunday.Contract       38.24       38.24
 100  Sunday.Market         43.24       43.24
 101  Saturday.Contract     38.24       46.70
 102  Saturday.Market       43.24       51.70
 103  Weekday.Contract      38.24       55.05
 104  Weekday.Market        43.24       60.05;
 105   
 106  Table Nobugflow_Rel(tot_vol,Days,p)"Observed releases of different monthly
       volume on daytypes d and period p  (cfs)"
 107  *V1 The release volume of March 2016 was ~0.72 MAF.
 108  *V2 The release volume of August 2015 was ~0.83 MAF.
 109  *V3 The release volume of August 2017 was ~0.94 MAF.
 110                   pLow        pHigh
 111  V1.Sunday        9171.4       9685.1
 112  V1.Saturday      9559.4      11452.5
 113  V1.Weekday       9702.1      13081.8
 114  V2.Sunday       10535.6      12431.2
 115  V2.Saturday     11461.6      13451.1
 116  V2.Weekday      10983.1      15029.9
 117  V3.Sunday       12820.3      13802.0
 118  V3.Saturday     13039.8      15509.4
 119  V3.Weekday      13115.5      16659.9    ;
 120  *===============================================
 121  SCALAR
 122  Convert                        Conversion factor from cfs to ac-ft per hou
      r (0.0014*60)/0.083/
 123  Daily_RelRange                 Allowable daily release range (cfs)/8000/
 124   
 125  Totaldays                      Total number of days in the month/30/
 126  Nu_Saturdays                   Number of saturdays in the month/4/
 127  Nu_Sun_Holi                    Number of sundays + holidays in the month /
      4/
 128  *Here we are considering an arbitrary monthly calender with exact number o
      f days as in real month but that considered month starts on monday.
 129  *Which means there will be 4 Saturdays and 4 Sundays in the month. We are 
      considering any holidays in the month.
 130  *The real monthly calender can be easily used by changing the number of da
      ys of each day type, if required.
 131  *===============================================
 132  VARIABLES
 133   
 134  ObjectiveVal                    Objective functions value ($)
 135  storage                         Reservoir storage at the end of the month 
      (acre-ft)
 136  Released_vol                    Total water released during the month (ac-
      ft)
 137   
 138  Revenue_zeroSteadyFlow          Revenue genereated from all flowpatterns d
      aytypes and periods when zero number of steady low flow day($)
 139   
 140  Positive Variables
 141   
 142  Revenue(FlowPattern,d,p)        Revenue all ($)
 143   
 144  Release(FlowPattern,d,p)        Reservoir release on different day types a
      nd flow patterns durinng period p (cfs)
 145  Energy_Gen(FlowPattern,d,p)     Hydropower Generated within each timestep 
      during different day types(MWh)
 146   
 147  ;
 148  *===============================================
 149   
 150  EQUATIONS
 151   
 152  *Constraints
 153  EQ1_ResMassBal                                   Reservoir mass balance (a
      cre-ft)
 154  EQ2_reqpowerstorage                              The minimum storage requi
      red for hydropower generation(power pool storage) (acre-ft)
 155  EQ3_maxstor                                      Reservoir Max storage (ac
      re-ft)
 156  EQ4_MaxR(FlowPattern,d,p)                        Max Release for any day t
      ype during any period p but it will not work when NumDays will be zero(cfs
      )
 157  EQ5_MinR(FlowPattern,d,p)                        Min Release for any day t
      ype with flows during any period p but it will not work when NumDays will 
      be zero (cfs)
 158  EQ6_ZeroFlowDays(FlowPattern,d,p)                No release for any day ty
      pe during any period p when Num_Days equal to zero(cfs)
 159  EQ7_Rel_Range(FlowPattern,d)                     Constraining the daily re
      lease range but it will not work when NumDays will be zero(cfs per day)
 160  EQ8_AlternativeDays_Relrange                     Constraining release chan
      ge between on-peak of current day and off-peak of next day to be less than
       or equal to 8000 (cfs)
 161  EQ9_AlternativeDays_Relrange                     Constraining release chan
      ge between on-peak of current day and off-peak of next day to be less than
       or equal to 8000 (cfs)
 162  EQ10_AlternativeDays_Relrange                    Constraining release chan
      ge between on-peak of current day and off-peak of next day to be less than
       or equal to 8000 (cfs)
 163   
 164  EQ11_Monthtlyrel                                 Constraining total monthl
      y release volume (ac-ft)
 165  EQ12_RelVolume                                   Total volume from differe
      nt types of day in the month (ac-ft)
 166   
 167  EQ13_SteadyFlow_Day(d)                           Constraining on-peak and 
      off-peak releases during Steadyflow day to be equal (cfs)
 168  EQ14_OffsetRel                                   Offset release between of
      f-peak unsteady weekday and off-peak steady weekend (saturday or and sunda
      y)releses(cfs)
 169   
 170  EQ15_OnPeak_Saturday                             On-peak Saturday constrai
      nt. i.e. Weekend on-peak minus 2000 cfs (found this value from observed hy
      drographs of 2015 2016 2017).
 171  EQ15a_offpeak_Saturday                           Off-peak Saturday constra
      int (cfs)
 172   
 173  EQ16_OnPeak_Sunday                               On-peak Sunday constraint
      . i.e.  equal to Saturday On-peak.
 174  EQ16a_offpeak_Sunday                             Off-peak Sunday constrain
      t (cfs)
 175   
 176   
 177  EQ17_Steady_Saturdays(p)                         Constraining the steady S
      aturday flows equal to steady sundays flows (cfs)
 178   
 179  ** here I am assuming that steady weekday equals to steady sundays.
 180  EQ18_Steady_Weekdays(p)                          Constraining the steady w
      eekdays flows equal to steady sundays flows (cfs)
 181   
 182  EQ19_OnPeak_UnsteadyDay(d)                       Constraining on-peak unst
      eady day release to be greater than off-peak unsteady release on the same 
      day (cfs)
 183   
 184  EQ20_EnergyGen_Max(FlowPattern,d,p)              Maximum Energy Generation
       Limit of the Glen Caynon Dam(MW)
 185  EQ21_EnergyGen(FlowPattern,d,p)                  Energy generated in each 
      period p during different day types (MWh)
 186   
 187  *Objective Functions
 188   
 189  EQ22_Unsteady_days                              Revenue generated during u
      nsteady Days ($).  For all scenarios except hydropeaking hydrograph--Zero 
      Steady low flow days($)
 190   
 191  EQ23_Unbounded(d,p)                              To tackle Unbounded ray e
      rror in case of flat hydrograph
 192  EQ24_Steadydays_Onpeak                          Revenue generated during o
      n-peak Steadyday ($).
 193  EQ25_Steadydays_Offpeak                         Revenue generated during o
      ff-peak Steadyday ($)
 194  EQ26_TotalRevenue                               Total monthly Hydropower R
      evenue generated($). The revenue has all daytypes and all flowpatterns wit
      h both market and contract prices.
 195  ;
 196   
 197   
 198   
 199  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
 200   
 201  *Mass Balance Equation
 202  EQ1_ResMassBal..                               storage =e= Initstorage + (
      Inflow*Convert*sum(p,Duration(p))*Totaldays)- Released_vol - evap;
 203  *                                                                         
       CFS * conversion factor from cfs to ac-ft/hr and multiplied by 24 (total 
      duration in a day) then multiplied by total day in the month
 204  *=======================Physical Constraints==============================
      =======
 205  EQ2_reqpowerstorage..                          storage =g= minstorage;
 206  EQ3_maxstor..                                  storage =l= maxstorage;
 207   
 208  EQ4_MaxR(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days(FlowPattern,d) gt 0)..                
           Release(FlowPattern,d,p)=l= maxRel;
 209   
 210  EQ5_MinR(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days(FlowPattern,d) gt 0)..                
           Release(FlowPattern,d,p)=g= minRel;
 211   
 212  EQ6_ZeroFlowDays(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days(FlowPattern,d) eq 0)..        
           Release(FlowPattern,d,p)=e=0;
 213   
 214  EQ7_Rel_Range(FlowPattern,d)$(Num_Days(FlowPattern,d) gt 0)..             
           Release(FlowPattern,d,"pHigh")- Release(FlowPattern,d,"pLow")=l=Daily
      _RelRange;
 215   
 216  EQ8_AlternativeDays_Relrange$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Sunday") gt 0)..      
           Release("HydroPeak","Saturday","pHigh")- Release("HydroPeak","Sunday"
      ,"pLow")=l=Daily_RelRange;
 217  EQ9_AlternativeDays_Relrange$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Saturday") gt 0) ..   
           Release("HydroPeak","Weekday","pHigh")- Release("HydroPeak","Saturday
      ","pLow")=l=Daily_RelRange;
 218  EQ10_AlternativeDays_Relrange..                                           
           Release("HydroPeak","Sunday","pHigh")- Release("HydroPeak","Weekday",
      "pLow")=l=Daily_RelRange;
 219   
 220   
 221  *EQ11_  constraining the overall monthly released volume..
 222  EQ11_Monthtlyrel..                                                        
            TotMonth_volume=e= Released_vol;
 223   
 224  EQ12_RelVolume..                                                          
            Released_vol=e= sum(FlowPattern,sum(d, sum(p, Release(FlowPattern,d,
      p)*Convert*Duration(p))*Num_Days(FlowPattern,d)));
 225   
 226  *======================Managerial Constraints=============================
      ======================
 227   
 228  EQ13_SteadyFlow_Day(d)$(Num_days("Steady","Sunday") gt 0)..               
                   Release("Steady",d,"pHigh") =e= Release("Steady",d,"pLow");
 229   
 230  * EQ14_  finds the minimimum release value from the hydrograph plus additi
      onal release we desire on weekends above off-peak weekday release (i.e. Of
      fset).
 231   
 232  EQ14_OffsetRel$((Num_days("HydroPeak","Weekday") gt 0) and (Num_Days("Stea
      dy","Sunday") gt 0))..                                       Release("Stea
      dy","Sunday","pLow")=e= Release("HydroPeak","Weekday","pLow")+ Weekend_Rel
      ;
 233   
 234  EQ15_OnPeak_Saturday$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Saturday") gt 0)..            
                         Release("HydroPeak","Saturday","pHigh")=e= Release("Hyd
      roPeak","Weekday","pHigh")-2000;
 235   
 236  EQ15a_offpeak_Saturday$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Saturday") gt 0)..          
                         Release("HydroPeak","Saturday","pLow")=e=  Release("Hyd
      roPeak","Weekday","pLow");
 237   
 238   
 239  EQ16_OnPeak_Sunday$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Sunday") gt 0)..                
             Release("HydroPeak","Sunday","pHigh")=e= Release("HydroPeak","Weekd
      ay","pHigh")-2000;
 240  EQ16a_offpeak_Sunday$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Sunday") gt 0)..              
             Release("HydroPeak","Sunday","pLow")=e= Release("HydroPeak","Weekda
      y","pLow");
 241   
 242   
 243  EQ17_Steady_Saturdays(p)$(Num_Days("Steady","Saturday")gt 0)..   Release("
      Steady","Saturday",p)=e= Release("Steady","Sunday",p);
 244  ** Eq 18 assumes that steady weekday equals the steady sunday releases.
 245  EQ18_Steady_Weekdays(p)$(Num_Days("Steady","Weekday")gt 0)..     Release("
      Steady","Weekday",p)=e= Release("Steady","Sunday",p);
 246   
 247   
 248  EQ19_OnPeak_UnsteadyDay(d)$(Num_Days("HydroPeak",d)gt 0)..                
          Release("HydroPeak",d,"pHigh")=g= Release("HydroPeak",d,"pLow");
 249   
 250  EQ20_EnergyGen_Max(FlowPattern,d,p)..                                     
           Energy_Gen(FlowPattern,d,p)=l= 1320*Duration(p);
 251  *Maximum Energy Generation capacity of GCD (MWH).. Source https://www.usbr
      .gov/uc/rm/crsp/gc
 252  EQ21_EnergyGen(FlowPattern,d,p)..                                         
           Energy_Gen(FlowPattern,d,p)=e= Release(FlowPattern,d,p)*Duration(p)*0
      .03715;
 253  * Energy generation formula used in WAPA Execl model..
 254   
 255  *==============================Objective Function=========================
      =============
 256  EQ22_Unsteady_days(FlowPattern,d,p)$((Num_Days("Steady","Sunday") gt 0)and
      (Num_Days("Hydropeak","Weekday") gt 0))..          Revenue("HydroPeak",d,p
      )=e= [{ Observed_Rel(d,p)* Energy_Price(d,"Contract",p)+ (Release("HydroPe
      ak",d,p)- Observed_Rel(d,p))*Energy_Price(d,"Market",p)}*0.03715*Duration(
      p)]* Num_Days("HydroPeak",d);
 257   
 258  EQ23_Unbounded(d,p)$(Num_Days("Hydropeak","Weekday") eq 0)..              
                                                           Revenue("HydroPeak",d
      ,p)=e=0;
 259   
 260  EQ24_Steadydays_Onpeak(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days("Steady","Sunday") gt 0)
      ..                        Revenue("Steady",d,"pHigh")=e=  [{ Release("Stea
      dy",d,"pHigh")* Energy_Price(d,"Contract","pHigh")-(Observed_Rel(d,"pHigh"
      )-Release("Steady",d,"pHigh"))*Energy_Price(d,"Market","pHigh")}*Duration(
      "pHigh")*0.03715]* Num_Days("Steady",d);
 261  EQ25_Steadydays_Offpeak(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days("Steady","Sunday") gt 0
      )..                       Revenue("Steady",d,"pLow")=e=  [{Observed_Rel(d,
      "pLow")* Energy_Price(d,"Contract","pLow") + (Release("Steady",d,"pLow")- 
      Observed_Rel(d,"pLow"))*Energy_Price(d,"Market","pLow")}*Duration("pLow")*
      0.03715]* Num_Days("Steady",d);
 262   
 263  EQ26_TotalRevenue..                                                       
                               ObjectiveVal=e= Sum((FlowPattern,d,p),Revenue(Flo
      wPattern,d,p));
 264   
 265  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
 266   
 267  MODEL Model1 Find value of hydropower revenue using LP/ALL/;
 268  *This model is for all cases of steady flow days. But the results of zero 
      steady low flow days scenario are incorrect so we need seperate model for 
      that.
 269   
 270  Loop((Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays),
 271   
 272  Weekend_Rel= Diff_Release(Offset);
 273  TotMonth_volume = Vol_monthlyrelease(tot_vol);
 274  Observed_Rel(Days,p)= Nobugflow_Rel(tot_vol,Days,p);
 275  Num_Days(FlowType,Days)= Days_Distribution(FlowType,Days,Nu_SteadyDays)+ E
      PS;
 276   
 277  option LP= CPLEX;
 278   
 279  Solve Model1 using LP MAXIMIZE ObjectiveVal;
 280   
 281  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      ---------------------------------------------
 282  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      ---------------------------------------------
 283  * All the following lines of code are saving values for different paramete
      rs
 284   
 285    FStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays)= ObjectiveVal.L;
 286   
 287  * XStore store the energy generated (Mwh/day) during different types of da
      ys
 288     XStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days)= sum (p,Energy_Gen.L
      (FlowType,Days,p))+ EPS;
 289   
 290  * RStore store the reservoir releases (cfs) during different types of days
       and scenarios.
 291     RStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days,p)= Release.L(FlowTyp
      e,Days,p)+ EPS;
 292   
 293  *Sstore store the end of month reservoir storage (ac-ft)
 294     Sstore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays)= storage.L + EPS;
 295   
 296  Rev(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days,p)=  Revenue.L(FlowType,Day
      s,p) +EPS;
 297   
 298  *Saving the model status for different scenarios.
 299     ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,"SolStat")= Model1.solvestat;
 300     ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,"ModStat")= Model1.modelstat;
 301   
 302    option clear=ObjectiveVal,clear=Release,clear=Energy_Gen;
 303  );
 304   
 305   
 306  *+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
      ++++++++++++
 307  * Model for Zero steady Low flow day scenario.
 308   
 309  Equation
 310  EQ27_ZeroBugDays_Revenue                         Revenue generated from al
      l flowpatterns daytypes and periods with zero steady low flow days($)
 311  ;
 312   
 313  EQ27_ZeroBugDays_Revenue$(Num_Days("Steady","Sunday") eq 0)..            R
      evenue_zeroSteadyFlow =e= sum(FlowPattern,sum(d, sum(p,Energy_Gen(FlowPatt
      ern,d,p)*Energy_Price(d,"Contract",p))*Num_Days(FlowPattern,d)));
 314   
 315   
 316  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
 317   
 318  MODEL Model0 Find value of hydropower revenue at zero steady flow days usi
      ng LP/ALL/;
 319  *This model is for zero steady low flow days only
 320   
 321   
 322  Num_Days(FlowType,Days)= Days_Distribution(FlowType,Days,"Case1")+ EPS;
 323   
 324  Loop((Offset,tot_vol),
 325   
 326  Weekend_Rel= Diff_Release(Offset);
 327  TotMonth_volume = Vol_monthlyrelease(tot_vol);
 328   
 329   
 330  option LP= CPLEX;
 331   
 332  Solve Model0 using LP MAXIMIZE Revenue_zeroSteadyFlow;
 333   
 334   
 335  * All the following lines of code are saving values for different paramete
      rs
 336    FStore(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1")=Revenue_zeroSteadyFlow.L;
 337   
 338  * XStore store the energy generated (Mwh/day) during different types of da
      ys
 339     XStore(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1",FlowType,Days)= sum (p,Energy_Gen.L(FlowT
      ype,Days,p))+ EPS;
 340   
 341  * RStore store the reservoir releases (cfs) during different types of days
       and scenarios.
 342     RStore(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1",FlowType,Days,p)= Release.L(FlowType,Days
      ,p)+ EPS;
 343   
 344  *Sstore store the end of month reservoir storage (ac-ft)
 345     Sstore(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1")= storage.L;
 346   
 347   
 348  *Saving the model status for different scenarios.
 349     ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1","SolStat")= Model0.solvestat;
 350     ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1","ModStat")= Model0.modelstat;
 351  );
 352   
 353   
 354  DISPLAY FStore,XStore,RStore,Sstore;
 355   
